{"id":2515,"title":"Interactive Volume Rendering with Ray Tracing","url":"https://doi.org/10.2312/egst.20061055","final_url":"https://diglib.eg.org/server/api/core/bitstreams/21a410a0-6838-41e2-9c88-f96ae19ecccd/content","year":2006,"kind":"paper","source":"openalex","doi":"10.2312/egst.20061055","arxiv":null,"sha256":"7a90c619384f7a2f80c82630a28bf0d55b31802c9d7340d8c1bc6c89a2b69e88","ctype":"application/pdf","text_src":"oa","fetched_at":1792903510.4263299,"text_chars":102770,"abstract":"Recent research on high-performance ray tracing has achieved real-time performance even for highly complex surface models already on a single PC. In this report we provide an overview of techniques for extending real-time ray tracing also to interactive volume rendering. We review fast rendering techniques for different volume representations and rendering modes in a variety of computing environments. The physically-based rendering approach of ray tracing enables high image quality and allows for easily mixing surface, volume, and other primitives in a scene, while fully accounting for all of their optical interactions. We present optimized implementations and discuss the use of upcoming high-performance processors for volume ray tracing.Eurographics 2006 - State of the Art Report","file":null,"marks":[],"links":["https://diglib.eg.org/server/api/core/bitstreams/21a410a0-6838-41e2-9c88-f96ae19ecccd/content","https://doi.org/10.2312/egst.20061055"],"cited_by":[{"path":"975-3d-gaussian-splatting.md","name":"3D Gaussian Splatting","k":1},{"path":"19-direct-volume-ray-casting.md","name":"Direct volume ray casting","k":1},{"path":"902-adaptive-octree-construction-with-2-1-balance-enforcement.md","name":"Adaptive Octree Construction with 2:1 Balance Enforcement","k":3},{"path":"1001-png-compression-for-gaussian-splats.md","name":"PNG Compression for Gaussian Splats","k":5},{"path":"1180-interactive-volume-visualization-via-multi-resolution-hash-e.md","name":"Interactive Volume Visualizati